                        "review": "It seems like a good game, and the developers were meticulous at making sure the details of the characters and events of the revolution were accurately portrayed. Honestly, it was the best representation of the revolution that I've ever seen in medial.\n\nThat said... you'll understand why I can't recommend this after you get to the last few days. The game is hard scripted to just s**t all over you. Want to try and play straight and honest? F you. Want to be corrupt and power hungry, F you too. The game tries to simulate agency and making important decisions, but then at the end it just burns through everything you've tried to do, all the work you put in, all the hard decisions. Doesn't matter, because it's hard-coded for you to lose those two dice games. It's hard coded to burn through the reputations you've been building for so long. It's hard coded for your wife to be a b***h to you, regardless of the things you've done for her. It's hard coded for family members to die in an arbitrary and meaningless way. The game doesn't give you agency, and it doesn't respect your actions or intentions at all. Maybe that's the whole message, but don't act like there's some way to navigate all this bullshit and then yank the rug out from the player DAYS AFTER THE ACTUAL TERROR ENDED just because you want your fictional villain to be the real baddie. \n\nAlso the main villain of the game is so contrived and boring. The big reveal left me rolling my eyes so hard. Seriously, what a waste of a plot line.",
